{{!-- CORE LOOP — the GM playbook's last spread: the core-loop flowchart and, facing it, the
      flow of play across a whole campaign. Reference only; nothing here rolls or is stored.

      Unlike the Moves tab, this page is not transcribed. The two flowcharts are the publisher's
      artwork, so the system ships neither of them: a GM extracts them from their own copy of the
      free GM playbook PDF with the "Import Book Art" macro, and module/gm-toolkit/gm-diagrams.js
      reads the world index of what that produced. Until then each figure draws a placeholder
      saying so, rather than the tab being hidden — a GM who cannot see the tab has no way to
      learn the diagrams exist.

      `data-tab="loop"` earns the rail's flowchart glyph; the icon table in stonetop.css is one
      flat list keyed by data-tab with no per-sheet scope.

      Each figure is its own <figure>, not a bare <img>, so the caption travels with the picture
      when the two columns collapse to one on a narrow window. --}}
<div class="tab loop" data-group="primary" data-tab="loop">
	<section class="sheet-tab">

		<div class="stonetop-gm-diagrams">
			{{#each stonetop.diagrams}}
			<figure class="stonetop-gm-diagram">
				<figcaption class="stonetop-gm-diagram-caption">
					<strong class="stonetop-gm-diagram-title">{{caption}}</strong>
					<span class="stonetop-gm-diagram-note">{{note}}</span>
				</figcaption>
				{{#if src}}
				{{!-- Click to open at full size. The flowcharts are ~2000px tall and the tab shows
				      them at a few hundred, which is legible for finding your place but not for
				      reading a box. --}}
				<a class="stonetop-gm-diagram-zoom" href="{{src}}" target="_blank" rel="noopener"
				   data-tooltip="{{localize "stonetop.gmToolkit.loop.zoom"}}">
					<img class="stonetop-gm-diagram-img" src="{{src}}" alt="{{caption}}">
				</a>
				{{else}}
				<div class="stonetop-gm-diagram-missing">
					<p>{{localize "stonetop.gmToolkit.loop.missing"}}</p>
					{{!-- `@root`, because inside {{#each}} the context is the diagram: a bare
					      `stonetop.isGM` resolves against that, finds nothing, and silently
					      renders no button at all. --}}
					{{#if @root.stonetop.isGM}}
					<button type="button" class="stonetop-gm-diagram-import">
						<i class="fas fa-images"></i> {{localize "stonetop.gmToolkit.loop.import"}}
					</button>
					{{/if}}
				</div>
				{{/if}}
			</figure>
			{{/each}}
		</div>

	</section>
</div>
